        <!-- FAQ -->
        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>Which treadmills work with Apple GymKit?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Few home treadmills do. Among current models, the Bowflex T6 and T9, the Horizon 7.0 AT and the Life Fitness Run CX with the Track Connect 2.0 console are confirmed by their makers. Apple does not publish a list of compatible machines, so look for "Connects to Apple Watch" or GymKit on the exact model and console, and check the manual.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Can I use my Apple Watch on any treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Yes. Start an Indoor Run or Indoor Walk in the Workout app on any treadmill. Heart rate is measured as usual, and distance is estimated from the watch's motion sensors because there is no GPS indoors. The estimate can be off, especially if you hold the handrails, so correct the distance at the end when it matters.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What is the difference between GymKit and Bluetooth FTMS?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              GymKit pairs the watch directly with the treadmill so both share one workout: treadmill distance and speed on the watch, watch heart rate on the console. FTMS is an open Bluetooth standard that sends treadmill data to apps such as Zwift or Kinomap on a phone or tablet. A treadmill can have FTMS without GymKit, and a Bluetooth logo alone tells you neither.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Is GymKit more accurate than an Indoor Run?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              For distance and pace, usually, because it takes the treadmill's figures instead of estimating from your wrist. But it copies the treadmill's errors too: if the belt speed reads high, your watch records the same mistake every time. Check the belt speed with a mark and a stopwatch in the first week, and heart rate is identical either way.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Does the Horizon 7.4 AT or 7.8 AT work with Apple Watch?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Not by tap-to-pair. Horizon's own comparison table lists the 7.0 AT as its only current model with Apple GymKit and marks the 7.4 AT and 7.8 AT as not connecting to Apple Watch or Samsung Galaxy Watch. You can still record an Indoor Run on either, and both broadcast over Bluetooth to apps.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Do I need Apple Fitness+ to use GymKit on a treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              No. GymKit pairing and recording a workout need no subscription. Bowflex's manuals include separate steps for running an Apple Fitness+ treadmill workout with the watch paired, and Fitness+ is a paid Apple service, so check the current price if you want it. None of the treadmills on this page needs a subscription to work.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

